  m_Name: Day3Dad
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  Category: 2
  Prefab: {fileID: 6625514644646704096, guid: 1f6a6789373206e498f996cb54aeedb1, type: 3}
  Interactable: {fileID: 5048261325816738630, guid: 1f6a6789373206e498f996cb54aeedb1, type: 3}
  TextFields:
  - Dear Astrid,
  - "Things at the South Pole are the same. Bright all day, every day. No nights.
    Cold. Getting IceCube back online is a lot of work\u2014but the good kind. After
    two years of backup generators, stale rations, expired candy bars, and about
    a million games of cribbage, I\u2019m glad to be doing real science again.\r\n\nYou
    asked what happened with the CME and why it caused so much damage. You\u2019re
    right\u2014usually we shut the grid down to stay safe. That\u2019s the standard
    drill. The first burst from the sun wasn\u2019t anything unusual. We got the
    alert, ran the protocol, powered things down. Just space weather.\r\n\nBut then
    the second wave hit. No warning. Stronger, faster, and it struck right as systems
    were coming back online. Total overload. Nothing caused it. Just nature doing
    its thing\u2014a rare one-two punch from the sun.\r\n\nThere were people who
    warned this could happen. One of them was the guy who built the satellite Elijah\u2019s
    been trying to connect to. Most folks thought he was brilliant but eccentric.
    He died early on, but he left the project to Elijah. Now people are starting
    to wonder if he was right. I think he was\u2014about this, anyway. Not sure about
    everything else.\r\nThe auroras have everyone on edge. They\u2019re beautiful,
    but after the blackout, people don\u2019t trust the sky. There are rumors, stories,
    superstitions. Some folks won\u2019t even go out at night.\r\nWe\u2019re lucky
    IceCube was offline when the second wave hit. That probably saved it. And thankfully,
    the backup generators held.\r\nGot to go, Little Bear. I love you. I love logging
    on and seeing the work you\u2019re doing. I hate how closely everything\u2019s
    being monitored. The radio waves are supposed to be for emergencies only, but
    half of it\u2019s just pirate stations now. Honestly, they should give us more
    space to talk. Science isn\u2019t just data\u2014it\u2019s relationships too."
  - Love, Dad
  StreamingVisuals: []
